# Uploaded through the webapp (webapp/app.py): the master spreadsheet copy
# and the raw unit-glossary PDFs a user drops in via /map/<grade>. Both are
# regenerable by re-uploading -- data/unit_glossary_parsed/ (the parser's
# output, small JSON) is what's actually committed as source of truth, the
# same way data/unit_glossary_original/ is for the original 6 grades.
data/_uploaded_master.xlsx
data/unit_pdfs/

# Regenerable build artifact (not source): comes from extract_data.py
# against the sheet. Keeping this out of git keeps the repo (and any handoff
# bundle of it) small -- see README.md.
assets/images/

# templates/fonts/*.otf and templates/fonts.css (the real, licensed
# Castledown Pro / Benton Sans files) ARE committed -- this repo is private,
# so that's no longer a redistribution problem. If this repo is ever made
# public again, re-add those two paths here first.
